message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite the associated article. The author fields below are
  PLACEHOLDERS: the manuscript file supplied with this repository contains no author block, and the
  author list was deliberately not reconstructed. Replace every placeholder before release.
title: AURKB-PDAC computational workflow
abstract: >-
  Executed computational notebooks and reproducibility documentation for a chemotype-aware QSAR-GCN
  consensus screening study prioritizing natural-product-derived AURKB-targeting candidates for
  pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma. Covers COCONUT natural-product prescreening (738,827 records
  reduced to 86,056 compounds), descriptor-based classical QSAR with scaffold-disjoint validation and
  a hash-verified 6,232-row transfer, and DeepChem graph convolutional network validation with
  QSAR-GCN consensus prioritization yielding 615 Tier 1 and 29 Tier 1A candidates. Notebooks are
  supplied as executed, with original outputs retained.
